## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CKNE implementation in multi-tenant data-export scenarios, requiring clear resource mapping, dynamic reallocation logic, and SLA preservation.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-resource allocation mapping
- Minute-granularity reallocation cycles
- Baseline SLA guarantees with fair preemption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simplified allocation function
function allocateExportSlots(tenants, maxSlots) {
  const baseline = 1;
  const allocated = tenants.map(t => ({
    ...t,
    slots: Math.max(baseline, Math.round(t.ckne * maxSlots))
  }));
  return rebalanceToMaxSlots(allocated, maxSlots);
}
```

## Test Plan
1. Verify baseline allocation: tenants with ckne=0.1 receive 1 slot
2. Test proportional scaling: ckne=0.5 receives 4 slots with MAX_SLOTS=8
3. Validate reallocation: low-CKNE tenants deprioritized when high-CKNE tenants join
4. Confirm SLA preservation: minimum 1 slot maintained during all scenarios

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CKNE-driven incentives in streaming, including how CKNE affects throughput, partitioning, and latency, plus a stable rebalancing loop and end-to-end validation.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-throughput/partition mapping
- Kafka partition rebalancing and windowing impact
- Baseline SLA guarantees with dynamic prioritization
- Telemetry, monitoring, and stability guarantees

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-mapping for CKNE-driven resource allocation
function mapCKNETokens(ckne, baseThroughput, basePartitions, kappa, lambda, minP, maxP){
  const T = baseThroughput * (1 + kappa * (ckne - 0.5));
  const P = Math.max(minP, Math.min(maxP, Math.round(basePartitions * (1 + lambda * (ckne - 0.5)))));
  return {throughput: T, partitions: P};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to design a CKNE-driven throttling system across a real-time, multi-tenant telemetry path, balancing SLA commitments with global health.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE health propagation across hops
- Per-tenant priority and budget management
- Minute-by-minute degradation policy and backpressure
- Payload schemas and validation
- Testing for bursts and SLA adherence

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo throttle by CKNE health (high level, not production-ready)
function throttleByCKNE(tenantId, ckne) {
  const bucket = getTenantBucket(tenantId);
  if (ckne.health < 0.5) bucket.reduce(ckne.sampling);
  // return true to emit, false to drop
  return Math.random() < bucket.sampling;
}
```

